WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.380
Wassup my well-read ballas?

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.860
This week we're getting insane in the membrane with the Tell Tale Heart by Edgar Allan Poe.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.320
The narrator of this story
definitely one tweaked-out gangsta.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.300
Not only is he always talkin like
he just popped 17 Adderalls,

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.260
but this dude just killed an old man
fo’ no good reason!

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.360
We'll get to that later.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.740
Our boy livin with an old man who
ain’t never done him dirty or nothing

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:40.680
But there’s somethin bout dis geezer that he just can’t shake: His fugly-ass blue eye. Brutha like,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:46.540
“Look, I love this dude, but that damn eye 
is ughhhhh. This fool got to go."

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:52.100
Completely normal, amirite? Well, according to the narrator, the fact that he can always keep his cool,

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:58.880
whether he icin a brutha or just talkin about it,
mean there ain’t no way he cray in da head.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.260
For seven straight nights he creep on that old man while he sleepin so he can smoke him.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:06.400
But don’t be thinkin that he was too 
scared to do it the first time –

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:12.640
problem was da man’s evil-ass eye was shut every time he came in, so the narrator didn’t do nuthin.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:18.520
On the eighth night, things go ham. His nuts swell to the size of watermelons, and he's all like,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.600
“time to stop f**kin’ around. Let’s do this sh*t."

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.400
Cept he f**ks up da entrance and makin da 
geezer call out, “Who dat? Who's there?”

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.080
and opens up his freaky deaky eye. 
With the sound of the old man’s heart

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:35.080
bangin through his ears, the narrator seen that eye,
gets all riled up, and mercs dat fool.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.280
Cold-blooded.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.900
After choppin him up and hidin da
body parts under the flo – even mo cold-blooded –

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:44.760
the 5-0 roll in cuz somebody heard some screaming.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:51.300
The narrator playin it real cool til he think he hears the old man’s heart beatin. Da fuzz don't hear nuttin tho.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.880
That heartbeat gets louder and louder and be
doggin him so raw that he breaks down,

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.000
straight loses his shit, and fesses up to the popo.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.340
Peep this irony, playbizzle:

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.340
The narrator start goin off tryin to defend himself like he bein accused of doin some crazy sh*t.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.320
Thing is, it ain’t murder he freakin out about.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.920
He flippin out cuz folks callin him crazy even
though he think he normal as they come.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.380
And hows he gonna prove that to us? By confessing to a murder like it ain’t no thang.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:22.740
Nice. Good job.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:27.220
Our boy’s defense don’t get no better after 
we find out the only reason he hatin

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:31.000
is cuz ol’ crusty crust got an “Evil Eye" –
whatever the hell that is.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:36.500
Some peeps think that eye is a symbol for self-knowledge – that the old dude’s eye is just a reminder

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.200
to the narrator bout all the
wackness he got inside himself.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.580
Other scholars gettin their Freud on and say that the narrator icin this bruh

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.180
to show that he got power over a father figure.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.880
One of my favorites, though, is a feminist reading
where some folks point out that the narrator

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:56.960
could be a woman. She just so damn tired of bein objectified by a privileged old white dude

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.300
that she gonna put dat sucka in his place.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.480
STREET JUSTICE.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.690
Dat beatin heart got all sorts of interpretations too.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:07.980
Maybe it’s supernatural, and we got
some creepy ghost sh*t goin on up in here.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:13.680
Maybe it’s all in da narrator’s head and just further shows that there’s somethin dark and nasty inside him.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:19.320
Then again, maybe he's actually hearin somethin, 
and it’s just a bunch of bugs gettin their freak nasty on.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:24.920
When the narrator drops in the old man’s room, he talks about sittin up listenin to things called “Death Watches."

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.040
What’s a death watch?
A G named Thompson lay it down real nice for us:

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.900
"Two or more species of beetles
that gnaw in walls and old furniture.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.920
During their mating season, they signal by 
bumping their heads against solid objects,

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:41.040
the sound of which superstitiously
came to be called the 'death watch,'

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.700
foretelling the death of someone in the house... contemporary descriptions of the rhythmic sounds

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.980
of these beetles...seem to match
the rhythms of one's own pulse."

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:55.380
I guess if I had to listen to a bunch of bugs goin at it all night erry night, I’d go pretty crazy too.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.100
Ughhh.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.120
And speaking of crazy, you’d be damn insane not to check out the Thug Notes store

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:04.220
and cop some of my sweet swag.
See y’all next week, my well-read ballas.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.920
Sparky Sweets out. Peace!

